# Speech fixtures for the wake word. Regenerate with
#   node test/tools/wake-truth.js --make-fixtures
# The transcripts they produced are committed in test/wake.test.js, which is
# what the suite actually asserts against, so the audio itself need not be.
test/fixtures/wake/

# Reference projects consulted while building the describe-to-find and cloud
# features. Deliberately NOT committed, for two reasons:
#
#   1. file-brain-main is GPLv3 and NexaFiles is MIT. Committing its source into
#      this repository would put GPL-licensed code in an MIT tree. The
#      architectural ideas taken from it were reimplemented from scratch; no
#      file was copied, which is what keeps NexaFiles MIT.
#   2. It is 20 MB of somebody else's source and belongs in neither the history
#      nor a release.
#
# What was taken from them, and what was deliberately left, is recorded in
# FEATURES_ADDED.txt.
addon/
